#: ../../source/docs/rover-px4-quickstart.rst:67
#: d40d2c87ae9c452ead5611c0413bf34d
msgid "**The board must have its automatic Safety disengaged before the Rover can be driven.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-px4-quickstart.rst:69
#: 9809a8b1b11a48288add9678f7442220
msgid "**Safety Button LED Indications:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-px4-quickstart.rst:71
#: 4262cc79a9174072bf14fdc0df1d6c50
msgid "Fast Blinking indicates: Error Condition, Safety cannot be disengaged. Possibly not calibrated or sensor error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-px4-quickstart.rst:73
#: 6db4012c1e244aa29a23ab397d21f782
msgid "Slow Blinking indicates: Safe condition. Safety can be disengaged by depressing Safety Button for 5 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-px4-quickstart.rst:75
#: 710f6936af58477aa7b4a06c8c5741a9
msgid "LED Continuously on indicates: Safety has been disengaged. PX4 controller may be armed with Throttle down and to the right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-px4-quickstart.rst:77
#: 320968ead2564f719eea6763a3cee1cc
msgid "When the LED is continuously on indicating Safety Disengaged it may be toggled back to a Safety engaged condition by depressing the Safety button for 5 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-px4-quickstart.rst:81
#: 91c7421d512647b39a60212923aceb42
msgid "**Both the Safety engaged and Safety disengaged conditions require the button to be held down for 5 seconds to toggle them.** This is a safety mechanism to prevent accidental disarming during use and to prevent accidental arming during transportation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-px4-quickstart.rst:87
#: 5e249f4fc93d48f09ff319ebb177e82b
msgid "Test MANUAL mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-px4-quickstart.rst:89
#: 046abe9abda340c2ac438a23ea4ca7e5
msgid "To test the Manual mode, put the Rover up on blocks, to prevent a runaway, turn on the R/C transmitter, power up the autopilot (depressing the safety button on the PX4FMU for 5 seconds to disengage the safety lock (LED solid on)), and when a 3D lock has been obtained"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-px4-quickstart.rst:94
#: f2c20ad6349f43e69ba1c2718a93e605
msgid "verify that when the elevator joystick is moved forward that the rover goes forward and vice versa, and that when the aileron joystick is moved to the left,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-px4-quickstart.rst:97
#: 5a7413d6e33b4c5b985888798660ff6c
msgid "the steering wheels go to the left and vice versa."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-px4-quickstart.rst:98
#: 82fc2da38ccb489c93a33140e4f6f8a8
msgid "A R/C receiver radio tester that can display channel PWM values can also be used to determine the throttle and steering outputs of the Pixhawk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-px4-quickstart.rst:101
#: 211fb629695444ebade3cc5ab4af674a
msgid "If either the throttle or steering channel is reversed, then the R/C transmitter channel reversing function must be used to reverse the appropriate channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-px4-quickstart.rst:106
#: 416aaa9319384a56a86c5d3c2c8861fb
msgid "Test AUTO mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-px4-quickstart.rst:111
#: 149770af38a443af85deece3153830db
msgid "To test the Auto mode at least one waypoint that is either to the right or the left of the home waypoint must be loaded into the APM using the MP Flight Planner:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-px4-quickstart.rst:115
#: 55a72d39e80f47d88a4fb19e99b6c51e
msgid "Using the same test setup as in the Manual mode, verify using the Manual mode that the Rover throttle and steering are still functional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-px4-quickstart.rst:118
#: f9cbb62381864e3eb344fe6e8905fb94
msgid "Then moving the mode switch to the put the Rover in the Auto mode, verify that the Rover motor comes up to a speed commensurate with the Cruise Throttle value that was previously selected and that the steering moves to either the right or the left depending on where the first waypoint was selected relative to the home waypoint. If either the throttle or the steering is reversed, the Radio Calibration in the MP Configuration Tab (not the R/C transmitter) must be used to reverse the appropriate channel by checking the appropriate \"reverse\" box on either the aileron (steering) or the throttle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-px4-quickstart.rst:128
#: 0e6d481ab3aa4052a5a32236d3e992b5
msgid "Once the functionality of the Manual and Auto modes has been verified, use the Flight Planner Tab in the MP to setup a waypoint course. Make sure to set the Waypoint Radius to around 2 meters for good performance."
msgstr ""

